<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borre mound cemetery</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Borre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Borre mound cemetery, in Horten in Vestfold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, is one of the largest royal burial grounds of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a>, with great burial mounds of the 7th to 10th centuries. A ship burial excavated there in 1852 gave its name to the Borre style of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> art. The site is linked in saga tradition with the Yngling kings of Vestfold and is now a national park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borre-mound-cemetery.jpg" alt="Borre mound cemetery" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfmann · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BORREHAUGENE_Borreparken_Borre_Burial_Mounds_HORTEN_Oslofjorden_Norway_Steinst%C3%B8tte_Velkommen_til_Parken_Hauger_tr%C3%A6r_sommer_gress_etc_2021-07-08_IMG_8233.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
